 "notes": "E259 is the excavation-sheet row at the unit's own point (distance 0, bearing invalid); its components coded with grid E259 as the brief requires. Survey p. 536: burial caves on the site's northern slope coded N from the unit; one of them dated MB. Small baptistarium coded pool_def no. SWP Mem III p. 15 (Kh. el Khudriyeh) is this unit: 'traces of ruins' only. SWP Mem II p. 324 El Khudr ('east of the village of Taiyibeh') looks like a different place; it names no pool, pit or grave anyway: ignored. Source 4 (Callaway 1970) not accessed, no excerpts."
